# ROSE Compiler Infrastructure - Cursor Rules
# Source-to-source program transformation and analysis tools

## Project Context

ROSE is an open source compiler infrastructure from LLNL for building:
- Source-to-source program transformation tools
- Static analysis tools
- Code optimization tools
- Binary analysis tools

Primary languages: C, C++, Fortran, OpenMP, UPC

## Code Style Requirements

### C/C++ Standards
- Use C17/C++11 standards
- Follow CERT Secure Coding guidelines
- Apply COMPASS static analysis rules

### Security-Critical Rules (CERT C)

When writing or reviewing C/C++ code, enforce these CERT rules:

#### Memory Safety (MEM)
- MEM30-C: Do not access freed memory
- MEM31-C: Free dynamically allocated memory when no longer needed
- MEM33-C: Allocate and copy structures containing flexible array members dynamically
- MEM34-C: Only free memory allocated dynamically
- MEM35-C: Allocate sufficient memory for an object

#### Expression Safety (EXP)
- EXP33-C: Do not read uninitialized memory
- EXP34-C: Do not dereference null pointers
- EXP36-C: Do not cast pointers into more strictly aligned pointer types
- EXP37-C: Call functions with the correct number and type of arguments
- EXP39-C: Do not access a variable through a pointer of an incompatible type

#### Integer Safety (INT)
- INT30-C: Ensure that unsigned integer operations do not wrap
- INT31-C: Ensure that integer conversions do not result in lost or misinterpreted data
- INT32-C: Ensure that operations on signed integers do not result in overflow
- INT33-C: Ensure that division and remainder operations do not result in divide-by-zero errors
- INT34-C: Do not shift an expression by a negative number of bits or by greater than or equal to the number of bits that exist in the operand

#### String Safety (STR)
- STR30-C: Do not attempt to modify string literals
- STR31-C: Guarantee that storage for strings has sufficient space for character data and the null terminator
- STR32-C: Do not pass a non-null-terminated character sequence to a library function that expects a string
- STR34-C: Cast characters to unsigned char before converting to larger integer sizes

#### Array Safety (ARR)
- ARR30-C: Do not form or use out-of-bounds pointers or array subscripts
- ARR36-C: Do not subtract or compare two pointers that do not refer to the same array
- ARR37-C: Do not add or subtract an integer to a pointer to a non-array object
- ARR38-C: Guarantee that library functions do not form invalid pointers
- ARR39-C: Do not add or subtract a scaled integer to a pointer

### COMPASS Checker Rules

Apply these static analysis patterns from ROSE COMPASS:

#### Buffer Overflow Prevention
- Avoid sprintf, scanf, sscanf, gets, strcpy, strcat, memcpy without bounds checking
- Use snprintf, fgets, strncpy, strncat, memcpy_s instead
- Check buffer sizes before operations

#### Null Pointer Safety
- Validate pointers before dereferencing (nullDeref)
- Check malloc/calloc/realloc return values (mallocReturnValueUsedInIfStmt)
- Use assertions for pointer validation

#### Memory Management
- Allocate and free in same module (allocateAndFreeMemoryInTheSameModule)
- Set pointers to NULL after free (setPointersToNull)
- Check for new/delete mismatches (newDelete)

#### Code Quality
- Avoid magic numbers (magicNumber)
- Limit cyclomatic complexity (cyclomaticComplexity)
- Avoid deep nesting (deepNesting)
- One declaration per line (oneLinePerDeclaration)
- Avoid goto statements (noGoto)
- Provide function documentation (functionDocumentation)

#### Type Safety
- Use explicit char signedness (explicitCharSign)
- Avoid void* (voidStar)
- Avoid C-style casts (doNotUseCstyleCasts)
- Use const for string literals (constStringLiterals)

#### Floating Point
- Do not use float for loop counters (floatForLoopCounter)
- Avoid exact floating point comparisons (floatingPointExactComparison)

#### Signal Handling
- Use only async-signal-safe functions in handlers (asynchronousSignalHandler)
- Avoid using same handler for multiple signals (avoidUsingTheSameHandlerForMultipleSignals)

#### Forbidden Functions
Avoid these unsafe functions:
- vfork() - use fork() instead (noVfork)
- rand() - use random() or arc4random() (noRand)
- setbuf() - use setvbuf() (preferSetvbufToSetbuf)
- rewind() - use fseek() (preferFseekToRewind)

## Build System

ROSE uses autotools and CMake:
- ./build to generate configure
- ../src/configure --enable-languages=c,c++ --with-boost=/path/to/boost
- make -j$(nproc)
- make check

## Directory Structure

- src/: ROSE source code
- projects/: Analysis tools (compass, CertSecureCodeProject, CodeThorn, etc.)
- tools/: Feature-complete tools
- tutorial/: Example ROSE features
- tests/: Test suites
- docs/: Documentation

